IMPORT prelude

-- Sultan Hussain Ordinance 1904 (Singapore) -- the Kampong Glam land (s 2), the 30-year annuity scheme for the family of the late
-- Sultan Hussain and who may be paid under it (s 3), and the bar on assigning or attaching the sums payable (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SHO1904.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its Legislative History ends with
-- Act 23 of 1999 (Sultan Hussain (Amendment) Act 1999, in force 21 July 1999), G.N. No. S 61/2000 (appointed day 1 March 2000 "for
-- purposes of section 4A") and the 2000 Revised Edition. SSO's metadata calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0252 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The whole operative text (ss 1-4) is encoded; the Act is four sections long.
--
-- Not encoded: the preamble's history (it is recited, not enacted, though s 2 relies on it); the regulations made under s 3, which
-- were not retrieved, so the proportions of the annuity, the amount of any commuted gratuity and how it is calculated are unknown
-- here; the general law of State land that s 2 applies; and who counts as a "member of the family", which the text does not define.
--
-- DATES are whole numbers written YYYYMMDD (1 March 2000 is 20000301), so that ordinary comparison orders them. This is an encoding
-- device, not in the text.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sultan Hussain Ordinance 1904 -- the family scheme`

§§ `2 -- the Kampong Glam land`

-- s 2: "The said land situate in Kampong Glam, having reverted to the State, shall be administered by the Collector of Land Revenue in
-- the same manner as other State lands."
-- Preamble (recited, not enacted): the Court of Appeal on 23 December 1897 held that the land "must be considered as Crown land ... as
-- having been occupied by the said Tunku Allum without legal right or title".
DECLARE Land IS ONE OF
    `the Kampong Glam land`
    `other State land`

DECLARE Administrator IS ONE OF
    `the Collector of Land Revenue`
    `the family of the late Sultan Hussain`

GIVEN `the land` IS A Land
GIVETH AN Administrator
`who administers the land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `the Kampong Glam land` THEN `the Collector of Land Revenue`
    OTHERWISE `the Collector of Land Revenue`

§§ `3(1) -- the scheme sum and its period`

-- s 3(1): "The Minister may by regulations provide for the establishment of a scheme for the payment of an annuity to the family of
-- the late Sultan Hussain a sum of $350,000 for a period of 30 years from 1 March 2000."
-- The sentence is ungrammatical and does not say whether $350,000 is paid each year or in all. It is encoded as a figure only.
-- The period is read as running from 1 March 2000 up to but not including 1 March 2030 (an inference: the text gives no end date).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the scheme sum` MEANS 350000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the scheme start date` MEANS 20000301

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the scheme end date` MEANS 20300301

GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date is within the scheme period` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST `the scheme start date`
    AND `the date` LESS THAN `the scheme end date`

§§ `3(2) -- who may be paid`

-- s 3(2): "The annuity under the scheme ... shall be paid only to members of the family of the late Sultan Hussain who before
-- 4 May 1999 were receiving an annuity under the Ordinance."
-- 4 May 1999 is the First Reading of the Bill for Act 23 of 1999 (Legislative History). "Before" is read strictly: an annuity first
-- received on 4 May 1999 does not qualify.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is a member of the family of the late Sultan Hussain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was receiving an annuity under the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the earlier annuity was first received` IS A NUMBER
    `has opted for a commuted gratuity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has died` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the eligibility cut-off date` MEANS 19990504

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is eligible for the scheme annuity` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is a member of the family of the late Sultan Hussain`
    AND `the claimant`'s `was receiving an annuity under the Ordinance`
    AND `the claimant`'s `date the earlier annuity was first received` LESS THAN `the eligibility cut-off date`

§§ `3(3) -- what the regulations may provide`

-- s 3(3): "Regulations made under this section may provide for -- (a) the determination of the proportions of the annuity ...;
-- (b) the exercise of an option by a person to whom an annuity is payable under the scheme to be paid a commuted gratuity in lieu of
-- the annuity; (c) the payment of a commuted gratuity to the estate of a person to whom annuity is payable under the scheme upon his
-- death; and (d) generally giving effect to or for carrying out the purposes of this section."
-- Adding beneficiaries or lengthening the 30 years is not in (a)-(d) and would contradict s 3(1) and (2) ("only"); encoded as
-- outside the power (an inference from "only" and "for a period of 30 years").
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `the proportions of the annuity`
    `an option to take a commuted gratuity instead`
    `a commuted gratuity to the estate on death`
    `generally carrying out the purposes of the section`
    `adding a family member born after 4 May 1999`
    `extending the scheme beyond 30 years`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulations may provide for` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `adding a family member born after 4 May 1999` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `extending the scheme beyond 30 years` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- What the scheme pays a claimant at a date, ASSUMING the regulations use every power in s 3(3). That assumption, and the order
-- below, are inferences: a person who has commuted is no longer "a person to whom annuity is payable", so (c) is read as reaching
-- only one who dies without having commuted.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a share of the annuity`
    `a commuted gratuity in lieu of the annuity`
    `a commuted gratuity to the estate`
    `nothing`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Payment
`what the scheme pays` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the claimant is eligible for the scheme annuity` `the claimant`) OR (NOT `the date is within the scheme period` `the date`)
    THEN `nothing`
    ELSE IF `the claimant`'s `has opted for a commuted gratuity`
         THEN `a commuted gratuity in lieu of the annuity`
         ELSE IF `the claimant`'s `has died`
              THEN `a commuted gratuity to the estate`
              ELSE `a share of the annuity`

§§ `4 -- not assignable or attachable`

-- s 4: "The sums payable to the family of the late Sultan Hussain under this Ordinance shall not be assignable or transferable or
-- liable to be attached, sequestrated or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim."
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `an assignment`
    `a transfer`
    `an attachment for a debt`
    `a sequestration`
    `a levy`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the sum is payable under this Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is barred` IF
    `the sum is payable under this Ordinance`
